+"""Depth forcing (src/cotdistill/depth_forcing.py; train_student.py / eval_student.py --df-layers; arms DF, DFX).
+CPU, float32, a tiny random Qwen3.5 text model (8 layers, full attention at 3 and 7, the rest Gated DeltaNet, as
+tests/test_layer_loop.py) with the GPT-2 tokenizer from the local HF cache (its vocabulary gives the digit tokens
+the value encodings need). Checks: (1) with the feature off the letter logits and the loss are the plain A2 arm's
+bit for bit (and, with COTD_REF_REPO set, the trainer's history equals the reference checkout's); (2) at lambda 0 the
+gradients of the base weights equal A2's; (3) the captures are the listed layers' outputs and the supervised count
+per k matches the items' step counts; (4) the InfoNCE candidate set holds the positive once and the loss is finite;
+(5) 30 optimisation steps on 8 fixed items drive the probe accuracy at every supervised layer to 1.0 while the answer
+CE still decreases; (6) --df-shuffle gives every item another item's values, deterministically; (7) sidecar round trip
+and the eval_student probe path (subprocess, as tests/test_layer_loop.py); (8) gradient checkpointing on (reentrant
+and non-reentrant) gives the loss of checkpointing off within 1e-5; plus the digits target, flag validation, the
+token-budget loop and the value helpers."""
